      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Blood-injection-injury phobia symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Longstanding fear since childhood. Still very anxious around blood tests, injections, and seeing blood at work, including when talking about it. Reports nearly fainting whenever someone mentions needles, with sweating, nausea, lightheadedness, and feeling she might pass out; needs to sit or leave the room, especially during vaccination clinics. No actual loss of consciousness recently."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Avoidance of blood testing"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Avoiding her own care. Fasting blood tests requested approximately 4–5 months ago in the EMR have not been done; patient is unsure of the timing, thinking it may have been last month or earlier this year."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Depressive symptoms and sleep"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mood described as a bit low but better than last year; energy okay with some reduced interest. Sleeps 5–7 hours, broken, with early waking. Informal screening today: depressive symptoms present but mild, with function preserved."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Suicidal ideation"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies current suicidal ideation: “I get sad but I’m not gonna do anything.” Reports one past episode of passive suicidal ideation and no attempts."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Homicidal ideation"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No homicidal ideation."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Psychotic symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No psychotic symptoms, delusions, or hallucinations reported or observed."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mental state examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Alert, well-looking, mildly anxious, cooperative, and engaged. Neat appearance and good hygiene. Becomes tense and wrings hands when discussing needles. Speech normal in rate and volume, with slight hesitancy recalling history. Mood “a bit flat but okay”; affect constricted but reactive and congruent. Thought form largely linear, though vague at times. Prominent anticipatory anxiety about blood and needles. Insight and judgement reasonable; recognises fear is excessive and interferes with care."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Phobia-related anxiety"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Anxiety is highly situational in relation to the blood-injection-injury phobia. Patient feels the phobia may have increased lately and attributes this possibly to more coffee and TikTok scrolling."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Caffeine and cola intake"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports more coffee and too much cola at work; worries that cola is thinning her blood and making her more likely to faint with needles. Reassured this is not the case; caffeine may increase anxiety. Gradual reduction was suggested, aiming for no more than 2 caffeinated drinks per day."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Alcohol use"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports 4–8 standard drinks per week, sometimes more after a “bad day.” Advised to keep to no more than 2 standard drinks per day and have some alcohol-free days; alcohol can worsen mood and anxiety."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-17",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Occupational functioning"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Continues working as an administrative assistant at a local GP practice. Staff vaccination clinics and pathology pickups are very stressful due to needles; she sometimes swaps tasks."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-18",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-18",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Iron studies"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Last iron studies approximately 18 months ago per EMR; ferritin was low-normal. Exact value not available."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-19",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-19",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Blood tests"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No investigations ordered today due to time and the patient's avoidance related to venepuncture. Routine blood tests discussed: FBE, ferritin, UEC, LFT, TFT, fasting lipids, and FBG/HbA1c."
      }
    },
